Third-party software (declare dependencies — see LICENSE files in distributions)

ResumeCabinet is built with libraries that retain their own terms. Listed below
are the direct runtime dependencies declared in requirements.txt together with the
upstream license summaries commonly associated with those projects. If you embed,
redistribute binaries, or provide this application to others, verify compliance with
those licenses (sources: PyPI project pages or official repositories).

| Dependency     | Typical upstream license        | Remarks |
|----------------|----------------------------------|---------|
| flet           | Apache License 2.0               | UI framework (may transitively pull other OSS). |
| reportlab      | BSD-style                          | PDF generation (`reportlab` package). |
| deep-translator| MIT                               | Translation helper; may invoke external translation services at runtime — network/privacy considerations are separate from license text. |
| PyMuPDF        | GNU AGPL v3 (+ MuPDF copyrights) | **Copyleft**: bundling/linking implications for AGPL differ from permissive stacks; review AGPL if you distribute combined works. Copyright also applies to Artifex/MuPDF components; see upstream notices. |
| PyInstaller    | GPLv2 (+ bootloader exemption)    | GPLv2 applies to tooling; bootloader exception permits distributing frozen apps built with PyInstaller subject to GPLv2 bootloader terms — read PyInstaller’s current license wording. |

Flet/pyinstaller toolchain may install additional transitive dependencies at build or
install time; those packages are governed by their own licenses and metadata.
